11
00:56:34,285 --> 00:56:40,285
The Movie) is a 2008 jukebox musical romantic comedy film directed by Phyllida Lloyd and written
by Catherine Johnson, based on her book from the 1999 musical of the same name.

12
01:01:42,857 --> 01:01:48,857
The film features an ensemble cast, including Meryl Streep, Pierce Brosnan, Colin Firth, Stellan
Skarsgård, Julie Walters, Dominic Cooper, Amanda Seyfried, and Christine Baranski.

13
01:06:51,428 --> 01:06:57,428
The film follows a young bride-to-be named Sophie who invites three men to her upcoming
wedding, with the possibility that any of them could be her real father.

14
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Principal photography primarily took place on the island of Skopelos, Greece, from August to September
2007, with ABBA members Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus composing the film's score.

15
01:17:08,571 --> 01:17:14,571
premiered at the Leicester Square in London on June 30, 2008, before being released in the United
Kingdom on July 10, and in the United States on July 18, by Universal Pictures.

16
01:22:17,142 --> 01:22:23,142
It received mixed reviews from critics and was a box-office success, grossing $610 million
worldwide on a $52 million budget, becoming the fifth highest-grossing film of 2008.

17
01:27:25,714 --> 01:27:31,714
A sequel, titled Mamma Mia!

18
01:32:34,285 --> 01:32:40,285
Here We Go Again, was released on July 20, 2018,
with much of the cast returning.

19
01:37:42,857 --> 01:37:48,857
The film explores themes of single parent, parent child
relationship, greece, musical, romcom.

20
